# .agentigore — context filter Kimi (kimi-peer-adapter.sh)
#
# File name: .agentigore (with a dot, without 'n' before 'ore').
# Copy this file to the repo root: cp extensions/agentigore.sample .agentigore
#
# Patterns in the style of .gitignore. Kimi does not receive the contents of matched files
# as context when launched via kimi-peer-adapter.sh.
# Does not affect git — Kimi reads, git does not see.
#
# Three priority levels (arrange from highest to lowest):
#
#   LEVEL-1 — secrets and private data (always ignore):
#     .secrets/
#     personal/
#
#   LEVEL-2 — heavy context (ignore if there is no direct task):
#     docs/
#     archive/
#
#   LEVEL-3 — enabled by default (do not add without a reason):
#     (empty)
#
# Examples:

# --- LEVEL-1: secrets ---
.secrets/
personal/

# --- LEVEL-2: heavy context ---
# docs/
# archive/
# DS-*/archive/
